          "extra_snippets": [
            "I’ve had the privilege and honor of serving as Sift’s CEO for almost 10 years. Over that time, my role has changed with each stage of growth. The skills required today are very different from what was needed 5 or 10 years ago. For example, today’s role is much more focused on operating and scaling a 200-person global organization.",
            "I’m at my best when I can get my hands dirty inventing novel technology solutions to challenging customer problems, and I want to go back to doing this. To put it in musical terms, I was born a jazz musician but today’s Sift needs an orchestra conductor as CEO.",
            "We’re well into the bonus round of the startup adventure and I feel a deep sense of pride and gratitude for all that we’ve accomplished. It’s been an honor and privilege to serve as Sift’s CEO and now I’m delighted to hand the reins to Marc and get back to doing what I do best.",
            "As mentioned this afternoon at Sift Summit, I’m excited to pass the baton to our current President & COO, Marc Olesen, as our new CEO!"
